# Force LF for every script/text format this project ships to Linux, so a
# Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) never silently rewrites them to
# CRLF. Found live 2026-09-25: packaging/linux/run-as-root.sh was deployed
# via direct scp from a Windows working copy (not a git clone on the
# target, which pulls the clean LF blob directly), so it picked up CRLF
# line endings, breaking its shebang ("#!/bin/bash\r" doesn't exist) with
# a misleading "No such file or directory" from the desktop launcher.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.patch text eol=lf
clonezilla-patch/* text eol=lf
packaging/debian/pbsgo-gui-root text eol=lf
packaging/debian/pbsgo-gui text eol=lf
